{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the opening of its head shall be.</b> The opening of the me'il at its top — is the opening of the neckhole." "<b>In its midst.</b> As its Targum renders: כָּפִיל לְגַוֵּהּ — folded inward, doubled into itself, so that its fold serves as a border; and it was the work of a weaver and not with a needle." "<b>Like the opening of a coat of mail.</b> We learn that their coats of mail had folded openings." "<b>It shall not be torn.</b> So that it not be torn; and one who tears it transgresses a negative commandment — for this is among the count of negative commandments in the Torah, and likewise ״וְלֹא יִזַּח הַחֹשֶׁן״, and likewise ״לֹא יָסֻרוּ מִמֶּנּוּ״, said of the staves of the Ark."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:21.033354998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}